description: House rules for every agent working on Porch Light
alwaysApply: true
---

# House rules

- Plain words. No em dashes, no en dashes; use a comma, colon or period.
- No secrets, tokens or key values in code, commits, logs or chat. Env var
  names only.
- Nemotron is the only model family in the runtime path, reached only
  through Meterless Runtime (one OpenAI-compatible base URL). No other
  provider, no direct model calls.
- Zetaris is the only data path at runtime. The app never calls a data
  source directly. Ingest helpers download raw files untouched into the
  filestore with a checksum and fetched_at.
- Every model call and every data read is traced (model, mode, local or
  NIM, latency, tokens) and written to the audit log. Nothing secret is
  logged.
- No posts about the project before submission. No public URLs, no
  production deploys, no public previews. Any deploy happens only with
  Joe's yes, auth-gated or tailnet-only.
- The repo stays private until submission.
- Never invent numbers. Every number on screen needs a source and a query
  id, or a marked placeholder. Fixture values are labeled mock.
- Every cached data file gets a `.provenance.json` sidecar: source URL,
  fetched_at UTC, SHA-256, license line, fetch command.
- Never rewrite or backdate commits. No force-push to main; PR required.
- No new accounts and no spending without Joe's yes.
- Nemotron never ranks. The fixed formula in data/scoring/weights.yaml
  ranks; the model writes the reason.
